    "created_at": "2017-03-23T05:57:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-23T05:57:57Z",
    "body": "For statically compiled languages strings are immutable since if you include a given string in multiple source files, the linker will resolve them down to a single copy in the final binary. They also end up in the read-only data section of the executable. Makes sense to state strings and byte-sequences are mutable for JS.",
