    "created_at": "2017-03-23T06:05:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-23T06:05:12Z",
    "body": "Strings are not mutable in JS. This is about what we do in standards with strings.\r\n\r\nBut that does bring up an interesting point, if JavaScript strings (as defined by Infra in due course) become mutable, does that mean IDL always needs to copy? It might be better if we match JavaScript after all...",
